# Industry investigation

Three Australian online retail experiences were reviewed on 2 November 2026.
The investigation focused on the product page, colour and size selection, stock
communication, cart design and delivery information.

| System | Evidence observed | Useful pattern for Pop Culture Clothing |
|---|---|---|
| Cotton On | Product imagery, price, colour thumbnails, available sizes, size guide and free-delivery threshold are presented together. The cart remains clear when empty and recommends a next action. | Keep variants close to the price and show a simple cart state with a clear route back to products. |
| Kmart | Colour, selected size, size guide and a location prompt for stock availability are visible on the product page. Delivery help separates timeframes, carriers, costs and preferences. | Make stock location-aware where possible and divide delivery information into short, scannable sections. |
| ASOS | The page clearly marks the item as out of stock, keeps colour and size controls visible and changes the main action to “Notify me”. Delivery and returns are grouped by country and shipping method. | Use explicit stock states and change the action when an item cannot be purchased. Keep delivery and returns information easy to compare. |

